claimed: intent-state-the-framing — the defect behind this afternoon retraction, not a nice-to-have. Two measurements an hour apart disagreed because one embedded messages bare and the other with a classify instruction, and neither printed which; the disagreement was read as a finding and published before a re-read caught it. Make every live arm print its conditions -- embedder id, framing, split, corpus size -- beside its number, so a row cannot be compared against one taken under different terms. Shared helper rather than a convention: a convention is what I already had.
